  "claim": "The significance of the lions, about whom a fictionalized account provided the basis of the film that was inspired by John Henry Patterson (author)'s 1996 book, was their unusual behavior.",
  "evidencia": "Page: The Ghost and the Darkness. Sentence: The Ghost and the Darkness is a 1996 American historical adventure film directed by Stephen Hopkins and starring Val Kilmer and Michael Douglas.\nPage: The Ghost and the Darkness. Sentence: The story is a fictionalized account of the Tsavo Man-Eaters, two lions that attacked and killed workers at Tsavo, Kenya, during the building of the Uganda-Mombasa Railway in East Africa in 1898.\nPage: Tsavo Man-Eaters. Sentence: The significance of this pair of lions was their unusual behavior, such as the number of men killed and the manner of the attacks.\nPage: John Henry Patterson (author). Sentence: The book has inspired three Hollywood films - \"Bwana Devil\" (1952), \"Killers of Kilimanjaro\" (1959) and \"The Ghost and the Darkness\" (1996) in which he was portrayed by Val Kilmer.",
