        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5d667375-2996-5842-975f-84abb6ed16de",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Ghost and the Darkness; Bwana Devil; Killers of Kilimanjaro\n- People: Stephen Hopkins; Val Kilmer; Michael Douglas; John Henry Patterson\n- Animals: Tsavo Man-Eaters\n- Places: Tsavo, Kenya; East Africa\n- Projects: Uganda-Mombasa Railway\n- Topics: historical adventure films; fictionalized accounts; lion attacks\n\nFacts:\n- In 1898, the Tsavo Man-Eaters attacked and killed workers at Tsavo, Kenya, during the construction of the Uganda-Mombasa Railway in East Africa.\n- The Tsavo Man-Eaters were notable for unusual behavior, including the number of men they killed and the manner of their attacks.\n- John Henry Patterson's book inspired the Hollywood films Bwana Devil in 1952, Killers of Kilimanjaro in 1959, and The Ghost and the Darkness in 1996.\n- In the 1996 film The Ghost and the Darkness, Val Kilmer portrayed John Henry Patterson.\n- The Ghost and the Darkness is a 1996 American historical adventure film directed by Stephen Hopkins and starring Val Kilmer and Michael Douglas.\n- The Ghost and the Darkness presents a fictionalized account of the Tsavo Man-Eaters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a8f11e34-23a8-53c0-88d2-c58c757ea17b",
        "text": "Page: The Ghost and the Darkness. Sentence: The Ghost and the Darkness is a 1996 American historical adventure film directed by Stephen Hopkins and starring Val Kilmer and Michael Douglas.\nPage: The Ghost and the Darkness. Sentence: The story is a fictionalized account of the Tsavo Man-Eaters, two lions that attacked and killed workers at Tsavo, Kenya, during the building of the Uganda-Mombasa Railway in East Africa in 1898.\nPage: Tsavo Man-Eaters. Sentence: The significance of this pair of lions was their unusual behavior, such as the number of men killed and the manner of the attacks.\nPage: John Henry Patterson (author). Sentence: The book has inspired three Hollywood films - \"Bwana Devil\" (1952), \"Killers of Kilimanjaro\" (1959) and \"The Ghost and the Darkness\" (1996) in which he was portrayed by Val Kilmer.",
